 plasma fibrinogen and factor clotting activity with coronary heart disease and stroke</article-title><source>J thromb Haemost</source><year>2006</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>2405</fpage><lpage>10</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17002654</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1538-7836.2006.02221.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmidt</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Fagerberg</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>ApoB/apoA-I ratio is related to femoral artery plaques in 64-year-old women also in cases with low LDL cholesterol</article-title><source>Atherosclerosis</source><year>2008</year><volume>196</volume><fpage>817</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17337270</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.atherosclerosis.2007.01.017</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jiaa</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Baia</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Fua</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Xub</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Yanga</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Long</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Relationship between plasma HDL subclasses distribution and apoA-I gene polymorphisms</article-title><source>Clinica Chimica Acta</source><year>2006</year><volume>360</volume><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>45</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.cccn.2005.04.004</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Forte</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>McCall</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The role of apolipoprotein A-I-containing lipoproteins in atherosclerosis</article-title><source>Curr Opin Lipidol</source><year>1994</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>354</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7858910</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00041433-199410000-00007</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Banka</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High density lipoprotein and lipoprotein oxidation</article-title><source>Curr Opin Lipidol</source><year>1996</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>139</fpage><lpage>42</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8818510</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vadas</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Gamble</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rye</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Barter</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regulation of leucocyte endothelial interactions of special relevance to atherogenesis</article-title><source>Clin Exp Pharmacol Physiol</source><year>1997</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>A33</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9143795</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1440-1681.1997.tb03052.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Koga</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Otsuki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsumoto</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Saito</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Mukai</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kasayama</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Negative association of obe